WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:29.300
Arthroscopic ankle fusion is a minimally invasive
surgical procedure that fuses, or joins, the

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:34.480
ankle bones together.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.360
The ankle is the joint that connects the leg
and the foot.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:45.989
The ankle joint includes the two lower leg
bones, called the tibia and the fibula, and

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:50.010
the ankle bone, called the talus.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.399
Together the ends of the tibia and the fibula
create a mortis, or a slot, for the talus

00:00:55.399 --> 00:00:59.510
which forms the bottom of the ankle joint.

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:05.500
Tissues called ligaments and tendons support
the ankle bones.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:13.590
Ligaments attach bones to bones and tendons
attach muscles to bones.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:19.480
The ankle joint allows the foot to move up
and down.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.610
Articular cartilage on the ends of bones is
a smooth gliding covering that allows fluid

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:30.510
joint movement.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:36.399
Ankle fusion, also known as arthrodesis, is
a surgical procedure that joins the ankle

00:01:36.399 --> 00:01:42.140
bones together so they no longer move or rub
against each other.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:47.709
Doctors may recommend this procedure for conditions
that lead to severe ankle joint damage and

00:01:47.709 --> 00:01:49.459
pain.

00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:56.410
The most common condition is osteoarthritis,
also known as degenerative joint disease.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:02.430
In the late stage of osteoarthritis, cartilage
covering the ends of the bone is worn away,

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.430
exposing bare bone.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:12.090
This, along with the growth of bony projections
called bone spurs, causes swelling, pain,

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:17.239
and limited movement of the joints.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:23.150
Another condition that may require ankle fusion
is rheumatoid arthritis, where the patient’s

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:28.000
own immune system attacks the joints.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.069
Any condition that destroys the joint surface,
such as a severe bone infection or death of

00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:44.120
bone tissue, called osteonecrosis, may also
require fusion of the ankle joint.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.030
To begin the procedure, the surgeon will hold
the foot down with straps to be able to see

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.590
inside the joint space better.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.159
Next, two tiny keyhole incisions will be made
on the ankle.

00:02:56.159 --> 00:03:04.239
A small tube, called a cannula, with a camera
inside it will be inserted through one incision.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:09.180
Surgical instruments will be inserted through
the other incision.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:14.129
The surgeon will use the surgical instruments
to remove cartilage and damaged bone from

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:17.110
the bottom surface of the tibia.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:21.209
This will also be done to the top surface
of the talus.

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:27.599
After this, the surgeon will remove the arthroscopic
tools and foot straps.

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:33.629
Then two or three metal guide pins will be
placed through the bones of the ankle joint.

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:39.469
The surgeon will use the guide pins to place
hollow screws which hold the bones in place.

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:43.849
Finally, the incisions will be closed with
sutures.

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:49.329
After ankle fusion, the patient will no longer
be able to move the ankle joint.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:55.760
However, fusion removes the pain caused by
arthritic surfaces rubbing together and other

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.879
joints in the foot continue to allow limited
movement.

